                                        "glosses": [
                                            "the cutting ability of an edge; keenness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1f2e468f-7d85-3e53-b649-1cf93023da90",
                                        "entry_id": "561e243b-50c1-3cd3-8ccf-8c63e68e4583",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "the fineness of the point a pointed object."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b767dde4-f3d3-382e-8841-fa5f79d456e8",
                                        "entry_id": "561e243b-50c1-3cd3-8ccf-8c63e68e4583",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The product or result of being sharp."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c7650b6-88d9-48c5-a24b-5b5fc91801fa",
                                                "sense_id": "b767dde4-f3d3-382e-8841-fa5f79d456e8",
                                                "text": "The first thing that strikes the stranger is the sharpness of the curves on the metre gauge; it is not unusual for a long train to be travelling in three directions at once, and the engine is frequently in full view of the windows of the ninth or tenth carriage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd12f7ff-0e63-34d3-aee9-943e9ecdb0bd",
                                        "entry_id": "561e243b-50c1-3cd3-8ccf-8c63e68e4583",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "pungency or acidity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3281dd6-0dc6-3d99-a987-78093158909d",
                                        "entry_id": "561e243b-50c1-3cd3-8ccf-8c63e68e4583",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "distinctness, focus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b04a8b00-74d4-3af3-a9f1-7fee3dde4acb",
                                        "entry_id": "561e243b-50c1-3cd3-8ccf-8c63e68e4583",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "acuteness or acuity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f075ba5a-84f1-445e-9784-6f31398af9ca",
                                                "sense_id": "b04a8b00-74d4-3af3-a9f1-7fee3dde4acb",
                                                "text": "Mrs. PAGE is gifted with a pleasing voice, which is yet imperfectly weeded of certain sharpnesses, but seems susceptible of a wide range of melodious inflection."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64b7325a-bb59-4c32-9b9d-d66e0fa8e8c7",
                                                "sense_id": "b04a8b00-74d4-3af3-a9f1-7fee3dde4acb",
                                                "text": "A lack of match sharpness was perhaps to blame for Rooney squandering England's best chance after 27 minutes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6d46435-92d6-3e70-bf98-0eadd01c484e",
                                        "entry_id": "561e243b-50c1-3cd3-8ccf-8c63e68e4583",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "edge or blade"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae2dbae9-4f63-42b1-aa59-76ecffc0153f",
                                                "sense_id": "a6d46435-92d6-3e70-bf98-0eadd01c484e",
                                                "text": "CUT-WATER, or KNEE OF THE HEAD [S.] the ſharpneſs of the head of the ſhip, below the beak;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "564953dd-9e50-4ad3-8991-452dab581262",
                                                "sense_id": "a6d46435-92d6-3e70-bf98-0eadd01c484e",
                                                "text": "also thei smytiden bi the scharpnesse of swerd, oxun, and scheep, and assis."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
